.TH BPFCCTL 8 "October 2026" "bpfc" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bpfcctl \- show and inspect programs managed by bpfcd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bpfcctl
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ status
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-l ]]
.br
.B bpfcctl
.RI [ options ]
.B show
.I iface direction priority
.RB [ \-\-bytecode ]
.br
.B bpfcctl
.RI [ options ]
.B reload
.RB [ \-\-no\-wait ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bpfcctl
reads the state
.BR bpfcd (8)
keeps in
.I /run/bpfc
and checks it against the kernel.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The default. One line per program file: interface, direction, priority,
status, kernel program id and tag, a kernel check, and the file. Errors are
printed under the line they belong to. Statuses are:
.RS
.TP 22
.B installed
Attached and current.
.TP
.B pending-iface
The interface does not exist; installed when it appears.
.TP
.B failed
bpfc or the verifier rejected the file, or attaching failed. The priority is
empty.
.TP
.B removed-externally
Removed by something else while
.B on_external_change
is
.BR log .
.TP
.B replaced-externally
Replaced by something else while
.B on_external_change
is
.BR log .
.TP
.B reinstall-limit
Kept being removed or replaced; bpfcd stopped reinstalling it until the next
reload.
.RE
.IP
The KERNEL column is
.B ok
when the kernel has exactly the recorded program at that priority,
.B MISSING
or
.B DIFFERS
when it does not (bpfcd normally corrects or records this within a moment),
and
.B occupied
when a non-installed slot's priority holds some other filter. A file changed
or deleted since the last reload is marked
.BR "reload pending" .
.RS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Also list TC filters on any interface that bpfcd does not manage.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
Add install time, instruction count, hash and ifindex.
.RE
.TP
.BI show " iface direction priority"
Also accepted as
.IR iface / direction / priority .
Prints the record, the source file with line numbers and, for a failed
program, the saved bpfc output including the verifier log.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bytecode
Also print the program's bytecode as the kernel holds it (after verifier
rewrites), with helper calls named when
.I /proc/kallsyms
is readable. Requires root.
.RE
.TP
.B reload
Send SIGHUP to bpfcd, wait for the rescan to finish and summarize the
result, listing failed programs.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-wait
Only send the signal.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config " file"
.I bpfc.conf
to take
.B state_dir
from (default
.IR /etc/bpfc/bpfc.conf ).
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-state\-dir " dir"
State directory, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-color= { auto , always , never }
Colored output; auto colors terminals unless
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B status
exits 0 when every program is installed or waiting for its interface and the
kernel agrees, 2 when some program needs attention, and 3 when bpfcd is not
running.
.B reload
exits 2 when some program failed.
Other errors exit 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# bpfcctl
# bpfcctl status \-a
# bpfcctl show eth0 ingress 100 \-\-bytecode
# bpfcctl reload
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bpfcd (8),
.BR bpfc.conf (5),
.BR bpfc (8)
